# Bigint multiplication of large values

Multiplies two 30-digit values to verify arbitrary precision
multiplication far beyond 64 bits, producing the full 60-digit product
without any overflow limit.

>>> source
first: bigint = 123456789012345678901234567890
second: bigint = 987654321098765432109876543210

product: bigint = first * second
print(product)

<<< stdout
121932631137021795226185032733622923332237463801111263526900

<<< stderr
